 "audit": "Four strong-looking signals are corrupted, and I left them out: NOTCH2 in embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma (19/75), MED12 in ependymoma (15/81), NF2 in pilocytic astrocytoma (13/168) and BCOR in medulloblastoma (25/212). Inside those diagnosis-gene pairs almost every protein_change is impossible: either the residue position is far beyond the protein length (e.g. NOTCH2 p.E127469G, NF2 p.P21404E, BCOR p.D72230R) or the missense substitution cannot arise from a single-nucleotide change. The same genes look normal in every other diagnosis. The rows look fabricated or mis-joined, which also makes me less sure the rest of the file is intact. Other issues: about 18 hypermutated tumors (POLE/MMR-like, up to 15,731 mutations; mostly 'Glioma, malignant') would inflate long-gene hits, so I excluded them from testing. Cohort-wide recurrent single variants (C17orf80 p.S281R, HLTF p.Q898E, ZNF510 p.Q248E, CCDC168 p.Q1530*) look like germline or pipeline artifacts. Many diagnosis labels are vague or missing ('missing', 'Unknown', 'Neoplasm, malignant/uncertain', 'Glioma, malignant', 'Rhabdomyosarcoma, NOS'), so histologies are mixed and true frequencies are diluted. Many diagnoses have fewer than 15 cases. WES mutation calls miss fusions and copy-number events (KIAA1549-BRAF, PAX3/7-FOXO1, SMARCB1 deletions), so drivers are under-counted. The cohort probably pools several studies, so selection and calling may differ by diagnosis. No duplicate patients were found.",
 "agent": "opus-neutral"
}